    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 28 Nuns Island presents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial townhouse in one of Galway City's most sought-after and historic residential locations. Brought to the market by DNG Leonard & Heaslip, this four-bedroom mid-terrace residence extends over three floors and offers exceptional potential for those seeking a renovation project in the heart of the city.\n\nWhile the property is in need of modernisation and refurbishment throughout, its generous accommodation, prime city-centre setting and traditional character provide the perfect canvas for a purchaser to create a truly impressive family home or investment property. The layout is arranged across three levels, offering spacious and versatile living accommodation with four well-proportioned bedrooms and a variety of reception and living spaces.\n\nNuns Island is renowned for its unique blend of city convenience and residential charm. Located just a short stroll from the vibrant streets of Galway City Centre, the property enjoys immediate access to a wide range of amenities while maintaining a peaceful riverside atmosphere. The area is highly regarded for its historic streetscape, attractive period homes and proximity to the River Corrib.\n\nResidents benefit from easy access to numerous amenities including the city centre shopping district, cafés, restaurants, bars and cultural attractions. Educational facilities are within walking distance, including the University of Galway and several primary and secondary schools. Healthcare facilities such as University Hospital Galway are also nearby. Recreational amenities include the scenic River Corrib walks, the Claddagh, South Park and Salthill Promenade, all easily accessible from the property. Public transport links and major road networks are also conveniently located.\n\nProperties of this nature rarely come to market in Nuns Island. Requiring renovation but offering immense potential, 28 Nuns Island represents an outstanding opportunity to secure a spacious four-bedroom townhouse in a highly desirable Galway city location. Its three-storey layout, character and exceptional convenience make it an appealing prospect for owner-occupiers, investors and restoration enthusiasts alike.\n\nFeatures:\nPrime city centre location\nApproximately 1,300 square feet of living space\nElectric storage heating\nIdeal investment opportunity\nModernisation required\n\nDNG Leonard & Heaslip for themselves and for the vendors or lessors of the property whose Agents they are, give notice that: (i) The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not constitute part of, an offer or contract. (ii) Any intending purchasers or tenants must not rely the descriptions, dimensions, references to condition or necessary permissions for use and occupation as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. (iii) No person in the employment of DNG Leonard & Heaslip has any authority to make or give representation or warranty whatever in relation to this development. DNG Leonard & Heaslip accept no liability (including liability to any prospective purchaser or lessee by reason of negligence or negligent misstatement) for loss or damage caused by any statements, opinions, information or other matters (expressed or implied) arising out of, contained in or derived from, or for any omissions from this brochure."
      },
